Package: surfscape
Type: Package
Title: Composition and Configuration in Continuous Landscape Surfaces
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Ehsan", "Rahimi", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "ehsanrahimi666@gmail.com"),
    person("Chuleui", "Jung", role = "aut"))
Description: Tests how continuous landscape metrics, such as surface,
    texture, autocorrelation, entropy and lacunarity metrics computed on
    vegetation indices or other continuous surfaces, respond to changes in
    the values present in a landscape window (composition) and to changes in
    their spatial arrangement (configuration). A battery of controlled
    changes (spatial permutation, uniform shift, scaling, rank-preserving
    change of distribution shape and landscape-wide rearrangement) classifies
    any metric, including implementations from other packages, as
    compositional, configurational or mixed. Continuous neutral landscapes are
    simulated by circulant embedding of Gaussian random fields. The change in
    a moving-window metric between two dates is decomposed exactly into a
    landscape-wide compositional, a local compositional and a configurational
    component using rank-transfer counterfactuals and the two-factor Shapley
    value. Built on 'terra' with a 'Rcpp' window engine.
